      <memberdef kind="function" id="classAstAttributeMechanism_1a6c861957e66074799b5c1affa9781d01" prot="public" static="no" const="yes" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type><ref refid="classAstAttributeMechanism_1afc3ea302f3a2459d08542643ea8b8d4e" kindref="member">AttributeIdentifiers</ref></type>
        <definition>AstAttributeMechanism::AttributeIdentifiers AstAttributeMechanism::getAttributeIdentifiers</definition>
        <argsstring>() const</argsstring>
        <name>getAttributeIdentifiers</name>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classList" kindref="compound">List</ref> of stored attribute names.</para><para>Returns the set of names for attributes stored in this container. This can be used to iterate over the attributes, as in:</para><para><programlisting filename="binaryAttribute.C"></programlisting> Or using the SgNode API for attributes:</para><para><programlisting filename="binaryAttribute.C"></programlisting> <bold>New semantics:</bold> The old implementation also returned some names that had no attribute values. For instance, if <computeroutput>operator</computeroutput>[] was invoked for an attribute that didn&apos;t exist then that name was also returned. </para>        </detaileddescription>
